  "scientific_conclusion": [
    "The body-preservation invariant worked: residual RMS is within five percent of truth in all three domains and rank-histogram total variation is at most 0.027, reversing the stochastic-body collapse caused by V41 global scaling.",
    "The frozen q99.9 residual-tail support is too narrow for the V41 object-amplitude target after block transport. Every one of the 768 candidate member-object pairs selected the minimum allowed lambda=1/64, yet candidate Q4 remains 137.9, 505.6, and 134.4 in TNG100, SIMBA, and Swift.",
    "Actual native-risk placement worsens Q3 and Q4 relative to both block-only and periodically rolled native-risk controls. A train-only classifier for present-day extreme-density locations is therefore not, by itself, a compatible rule for placing donor conditional-residual extremes on a query backbone.",
    "The remaining high-k excess is modest compared with V41's collapse, but the candidate still fails the upper high-k band, two-point morphology, and selected peak/void checks. It must not advance to an independent simulation gate.",
    "The next step is a diagnostic-only audit of train-only conditional tail thresholds, attainable amplitude intervals, backbone/body contributions, and held-out object-amplitude prediction error before any model or generator change."
